                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237857328",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198000807456",
                            "num_reviews": 238,
                            "playtime_forever": 41,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 41,
                            "last_played": 1792164012
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't even know why I initially bought this game. I guess I was attracted to the retro charm and music from watching someone else player it that I thought I'd give it a go.\n\nTurns out it's just not for me. I don't mind the gameplay and thought it was pretty interesting and fun up to a certain point. I soon realised it features what I counted were potentially 54 levels that you have to beat in one session back to back with limited lives and each stage gives you a 4 minute timer to beat it.\n\nIt features randomly spawning enemies that can literally spawn just as you're jumping to an area and instant kill you feeling very cheap, and the spawns are very sporadic and chaotic.\n\nIt quickly becomes extremely tedious and I just don't have the patience for it, unfortunately.\n\nIt's otherwise a very charming platformer, but the lack of save states and what I assume no check points once you lose all lives, just makes it not fun for me.\n\nI would not recommend this game unless you're an extremely avid platform player and don't mind repetitiveness.",
